    "decisions": {
      "D-029": "Daily attendance is the homeroom teacher's; it is not required of a guru mapel.",
      "D-263": "Completeness of each component comes from the one completeness service.",
      "D-278": "Berkas Administrasi profiles: Standar SIGRAK (default, S-01 order plus S-15 for a wali kelas) and Format Kudus (24 components for guru kelas, 18 for guru mapel). BK notes are never included.",
      "D-305": "Catalog copied from usulan-01 for one Tim Validasi review.",
      "D-367": "Curated with SIGRAK names, keys, and codes."
    },
    "conventions": [
      "Keys are English snake_case and never change once seeded; labels and other text shown to users are Indonesian.",
      "Codes follow SIGRAK-KAT-<AREA>-NN for the main items of a file and SIGRAK-KAT-<AREA>-<LIST>-NN for its secondary lists (see README.md). Codes are stable: a retired item keeps its code, and new items take the next free number.",
      "No identifier from the legacy app is carried over. Where a decision keeps an old label for reference (D-305), it sits in legacy_label and is never shown in the UI.",
      "review_notes are Indonesian notes for Tim Validasi SIGRAK; they are not shown to teachers.",
      "components is the union of both Format Kudus lists (24 for guru kelas plus 1 found only for guru mapel). label is the SIGRAK label shown in the app.",
      "profiles list the components in the Format Kudus order. format_label is the component name as written in the Format Kudus instrument (scale 1–5 in that instrument), used only when printing that profile. label on a profile entry overrides the component label for that profile.",
      "instrument_items name the SIGRAK supervision checklist items (S-01, S-15; docs/drafts/teacher-supervision-instruments.md, 0–2 scale) the component serves as evidence for. The mapping is a proposal.",
      "data_source says where SIGRAK takes the component from (table names from docs/final/data-model.md, feature IDs from docs/drafts/administration-features.md)."
    ]
  },
